    \centering
    \small
    \setlength{\tabcolsep}{5pt}
    \caption{
    \textbf{Features needed to retain the action-value difference.}
    Smallest tested feature dimension for which the TD-trained
    model reaches $\widehat G_r/G_r\geq0.9$.
    P11 uses the uniform policy; R1--R5 use sampled policies.
    A dash indicates that the threshold was not reached by $d=11$.
    }
    \label{tab:family-rank}
    \begin{tabular}{lrrrrrr}
        \toprule
        Method & P11 & R1 & R2 & R3 & R4 & R5 \\
        \midrule
        FB                            & 5 & 9  & 5 & 5 & 10 & 10 \\
        FB, normalized target         & 5 & 10 & 5 & 5 & 9  & 10 \\
        Softmax + squared error       & 3 & 3  & 3 & 3 & 3  & 3  \\
        \name{}                       & 3 & 2  & 3 & 2 & 3  & 3  \\
        \name{}, soft immediate target & -- & -- & -- & -- & -- & -- \\
        \bottomrule
